What is the output of the following code?
public static void main(String[] args) {
    for (int i = -2; i < 2; i++) {
        for (int j = -2; j < 2; j++) {
            if (i < j)
                System.out.print("7");
            else
                System.out.print("3");
        }
        System.out.println();
    }
}
The four output rows, top to bottom, are listed with slashes between them.

Consider these classes:
class Employee {
    public void displayInfo() {
        System.out.println("Employee Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("ID: " + id);
        System.out.println("Department: " + department);
    }
}
class Manager extends Employee {
    @Override
    public void displayInfo() {
        super.displayInfo();
        System.out.println("Team Size: " + teamSize);
    }
}
Carol is a Manager (name Carol, id 201, department IT, teamSize 5). What does carol.displayInfo() print?

